# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug/
target/

# Cargo.lock is tracked: avicoin is an executable, so a reproducible build and a
# CI run that fails for a reason visible in a diff both depend on it.
# https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/guide/cargo-toml-vs-cargo-lock.html

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# rulesync — source of truth is rulesync.jsonc + rulesync.lock (committed).
# Regenerate skills with:
#   npx rulesync install && npx rulesync generate
# Generated output for each target is derived, never committed:
.claude/skills/
.agents/skills/

# .rulesync/ is likewise derived — except the hand-vendored skills. rulesync keys
# its lockfile by repo slug alone, so it can only track one path per upstream
# repo; we point it at mattpocock/skills:skills/engineering, and these five (from
# skills/productivity) are committed by hand. /grill-with-docs delegates to
# /grilling, so without them it is a no-op. Living here rather than under
# .claude/ puts them in the generate pipeline, so they reach every target.
# See NOTICE for licensing. Update by re-copying upstream; they have no deps.
.rulesync/*
!.rulesync/skills/
.rulesync/skills/*
!.rulesync/skills/grill-me/
!.rulesync/skills/grilling/
!.rulesync/skills/handoff/
!.rulesync/skills/teach/
!.rulesync/skills/writing-great-skills/

# npm lockfile stub created by rulesync; there is no package.json
package-lock.json

# Python — the functional suite (docs/adr/0014-functional-test-suite.md).
# These were only in .git/info/exclude, which is local to one clone and never
# committed, so a fresh checkout or CI saw them as untracked.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
